to them the heroic  legend of the legendary second age will  be revived the series is supposed to  bring the view back to an era of great  powers falling and rising kingdoms and  unusual heroes and reveal the greatest  villain that ever came from tolkien's  pen  man is probably sauron although melkor  would probably object to that it follows  that the evil will grow strongly in a  time of peace and will have to deal with  an ensemble of old and new characters in  asian world last the whole map is to be  explored again there are a few theories  in this regard one of them is that we  can expect breathtaking open sea  adventures above all that's not unlikely  after all the island kingdom of numenor  is in the far south west of the map at a  point that only ships can reach by sea  the plot of the first of probably five  seasons will also be told in eight  episodes of still unknown length in the  teaser galadriel speaks the first lines  of tolkien's famous one ring poem it  says three rings for the elven kings  under the sky seven for the dwarf lords  and their halls of stone  nine for mortal man doomed to die  one for the dark lord on his dark throne  in the land of mordor where the shadows  lie  so far we only know the story of the one  ring from the movies but the series  wants to show us all of them in the  course of the story the children is jd  payne and patrick mckay have summarized  it quite well in the press release in  the series all the important stories of  the second age are told i.e the forging  of the rings sauron's path to power the  exciting story of numenor and then of  course the final alliance of elvis and  men which by the way is said to have  been one of the largest and most  glorious armies in the docking universe  also not to be neglected of course is  the cast at least three familiar roles  have already been officially confirmed  for the series on the one hand there's  the elf galadriel who will no longer be  portrayed by kate blanchet but by  morpher clark she's certainly one of the  most famous figures from middle earth  and now gets a significant rejuvenation  thanks to a 32 year old clark also  present are alron and of course the  villain sauron with elrond this time  being embodied by robert aramaio it is  also very likely that sauron as once in  the book will make use of his ability as  a shapeshifter one of these figures is  the character anatar who comes across as  very friendly but only serves the sole  purpose of convincing the elves to forge  his rings most of the casts consist of  relatively unknown faces they are for  example marcela cavanaugh who is to take  on the new character nori and joseph  maul who embodies the villanoran  meanwhile several dozen actors are known  but most of them haven't had any major  appearances yet  just as with peter jackson's trilogy  they chose beautiful new zealand as  filming location unfortunately as with  many other productions not everything  went smoothly due to the pandemic  filming had to be possible that up to  800 crew members were sent home and  production came to a standstill for  weeks for a project that is supposed to  cost over 1 billion us dollars as it is  this is of course no trifle fortunately  however production was resumed as soon  as possible and is still in full swing  by the way the large-scale project is  not filmed chronologically but very  efficiently with always several scenes  at one location of course it is only  possible if the script for season 1 is  finished because with this production  variant it is extremely difficult and  costly to reshoot scenes later season 2  however means saying goodbye to new  zealand because it will be produced in  great britain the responsible actors  behind the camera are on the one hand as  already mentioned johnny payne and  patrick mckay who both act as serious  developers and are the creative minds  behind the project the director  responsible for at least their first two  episodes was juan antonio bayonna known  from jurassic world in the subsequent  episodes wingnip and charlotte branstrom  will take their places in the director's  chair who definitely will not return as  peter jackson who refused to take a  leading position in the production he's  only to be available in an advisory role  what will also interest fans is the  budget which has already been hinted at  because calculated at 1 billion us  dollars the lord of the rings series  will become the most expensive series  production of all time the filming  rights alone are said to have cost 250  million us dollars not to mention the  huge budget for season 1 which is said  to be 465 million us dollars on the  other hand amazon will certainly receive  a nice sum from the new zealand  government because the streaming giant  is entitled to an estimated 116 million  us dollars from a national subsidy fund  due to the local jobs generated  [Music]  amazon's a true master of secrecy which  is why the rumor mill has a particularly  hard time finding valid information  however the streaming giant provided one  itself in the form of 23 pictures that  were posted at the beginning of february  discussing every single one in detail  will of course go beyond the scope but  there are at least a few clear pictures  that we don't want to withhold from you  first there's the image with a silver  and gold dagger and armor that alludes  to the dress of velanor it is an elf you  don't have to think along about the  picture where the figure is leaning on a  big hammer at the latest in combination  with the red beard and the golden dust  on the fingers it is clear that we are  dealing with a representative of the  dwarves a third picture raises more  questions because we see the staff of a  wizard which is supposed to represent a  broken sword if this is really a wizard  one wonders how he made it into the  second age after all they didn't  actually appear until the third age the  same applies to the figure with a scale  armor and the sword with a horus hand  here one immediately thinks of a warrior  from rohan although the realm did not  emerge until thousands of years later  last but not least a closer look reveals  a person with spy gloves and the sword  of sauron you can probably guess who  that could be furthermore some more  pictures were published shortly after  showing impressions of the new actors of  elrond and galadriel as well as some new  characters developed for the series  furthermore there are some behind the  scenes pictures which is definitely make  you want to see more  last sunday on the occasion of the 56th  super bowl there was finally a first  trailer to see because amazon in  competition with disney and netflix of  course did not miss the opportunity to  show the first scenes of their upcoming  the lord of the rings series finally  we'll give you some background  information that will surely make you  enjoy the new trailer even more first we  see footage of the island kingdom of  numenor as well as the voice of a young  girl who turns out to be a  representative of the so-called harfoots  played by michaela cavanaugh these are  one of the three original hobbit tribes  and even the largest in terms of numbers  subsequently it becomes clear that  during the series we will get to know  many places that have not yet made it to  the movie screen the characters that are  now seen are called nomadic hunters and  look quite like vampires with bad luck  wings are these possibly remnants of a  race from the first age we also see  gladriel played by morphet clark in  moving pictures for the first time she  seems to be quite reckless for example  fighting riding or even climbing in one  scene we also see her with a new  character a forest elf named aaron dear  in fact his appearance did not cause  enthusiasm everywhere as the dark skin  color of the puerto rican actor is very  much at odds with tolkien's original  conception of the elves well certainly a  debatable decision for tolkien's  hardliners in general the trailer  bristles with short fast cut scenes that  feature a monster-like creature  alongside flaming arrows and presumably  the elf celebrant boar actor owen arthur  plays prince durian iv a friendly  looking dwarf and son of during the  third king of gaza doom also known to  many as morion slowly we approach the  end of the trailer and can catch a  glimpse of a young elrond kneeling next  to a large rock and the dwarf princess  diese in the next scene we must look  very closely because we briefly see two  male characters one of whom seems to be  naked the inferno around them strongly  reminds us of mount doom in the  northwest of mordor and many speculate  that sauron can be seen here the trailer  finally ends with two dirty hands  touching which of course rolls out the  involvement of the extremely clean elves  left hand could be from the mysteries  tom bombadil being somewhere between  hobbits and humans his origin is a  mystery through and through he says of  himself in the first of the lord of the  rings books that he is older than any  creature in the world all in all this  super bowl gave us some great  impressions of the series the makers  didn't shy away from using a lot of cgi  which might not be to the liking of some  fans  that's it again with our latest original  we hope you're now up to date on the  latest developments and perhaps even a  bit more anticipation for the amazon  series than after watching the trailer  amazon's mega project the lord of the  rings the rings of power will be  released this late summer on september  2nd 2022 exclusively on prime video  [Music]  you

